  "body": "**Original comment by Paul Matthijsse (Bitbucket: [Paul Matthijsse](https://bitbucket.org/Paul Matthijsse), ).**\n\n----------------------------------------\n\n@{5e9f60be313afc0c1f0b361c} , in the Navigator you can use Ctrl\\+F, type your raw extension and hit OK, that’s faster than the Filter on Exif route.\n\nBut I agree that it would be nice to remember these filter settings in Filter Exif, even between sessions. A shortcut to activate them might be a good idea as well \\(@{557058:8f81e5da-fb6c-492f-84df-652b548f6648} , Ctrl\\+E \\[for exif\\] seems to be available, goes well with Ctrl\\+I for the Inspector\\). \n\nLast suggestion: I think people will be more inclined to filter on file type than on exposure compensation, so place the file type selector on top of the list.\n",
